1
00:00:16,480 --> 00:01:50,320
 Stars, galaxy, in astral seas above, on cosmic paths we'll trace, man over wings, he is such a wonder thing, behind us all come see, come take your place, we're leaving soon for-

2
00:01:50,320 --> 00:02:15,200
 Open land, there would see us eat, this pile of debris is gonna rust away.

3
00:02:33,170 --> 00:02:39,230
 Yeah, I'd like to rather describe this land as dangerous, full of wild animals.

4
00:02:39,970 --> 00:02:42,760
 Everything he's told you is true, you'll find that out.

5
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,440
 Knowing all that, you volunteered to come along?

6
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:46,020
 Yes.

7
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:50,170
 I don't understand. Why risk your life?

8
00:02:50,490 --> 00:02:52,040
 You see, Piero, it's like this.

9
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,680
 I should tell you that several years ago,

10
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:56,900
 the ones of the castle systematically eliminated our whole family.

11
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,440
 Only Giglio and I escaped.

12
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:00,130
 Now with you, there's a chance that we...

13
00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:00,410
 Quick!

14
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:21,020
 Just what I thought.

15
00:03:21,250 --> 00:03:24,400
 Cubies finally figured out that four weapons are better than one.

16
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:27,220
 Now they're coming after us to get the other three.

17
00:03:31,770 --> 00:03:35,220
 Two solutions.

18
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,820
 Either we wait in an ambush and wipe out all of them,

19
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:40,130
 in which case we can get our weapon back,

20
00:03:40,230 --> 00:03:42,140
 or else we change direction and we go that way.

21
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:43,770
 Second solution.

22
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,640
 Quickly, the fog will hide us.

23
00:03:56,430 --> 00:04:09,500
 Like this one, nobody's going to fess. We'll be all right now.

24
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:38,560
 Our friends are coming.

25
00:04:56,950 --> 00:05:06,410
 Well, that's that then. Let's go.

26
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:15,100
 Captain Pierro been found.

27
00:05:16,350 --> 00:05:19,230
 No, Great Computer. He has not yet been found.

28
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:21,590
 He must be found, Colonel. It is imperative.

29
00:05:22,910 --> 00:05:27,910
 At your orders, Great Computer, we will intensify all search operations.

30
00:05:48,850 --> 00:05:55,000
 Bikers are...

31
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,570
 It has nothing to do...

32
00:05:56,570 --> 00:05:58,130
 Those are men being attacked.

33
00:05:58,390 --> 00:06:00,410
 We can't allow men to be annihilated like that.

34
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:01,600
 They're used to it.

35
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:05,400
 I don't agree with you.

36
00:06:12,550 --> 00:06:18,910
 Stand guard, Metro, in case they come back.

37
00:06:18,910 --> 00:06:22,460
 Out on yours truly to receive them in an appropriate manner.

38
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:40,840
 They're showing their appreciation with this feast in our honor, but still they can't trust us.

39
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,520
 You see how they watch us? Suspicious.

40
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:46,060
 In this godforsaken wilderness, no one trusts anyone and stays alive.

41
00:06:46,690 --> 00:06:52,330
 This reptilian species, Saurian variety, they seem to be quite widespread over the planet in all their various forms.

42
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:55,870
 That is true, Metro. They are the dominant species on the planet.

43
00:06:56,360 --> 00:07:02,900
 These Ravagers are the most highly evolved, and I hope with all my heart that we won't be forced to come into contact with all the varieties.

44
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:07,360
 Ah, then you are in the Mesozoic era, I might say, secondary phase.

45
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:10,480
 The Jurassic period, Cretaceous, I cannot say precisely.

46
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:12,220
 An excellent analysis, Metro.

47
00:07:12,530 --> 00:07:15,890
 I'm forced to conclude that you are truly a mine of scientific information.

48
00:07:16,110 --> 00:07:18,530
 All right, we all understand that, but those are men.

49
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:20,870
 How can it be that they are still in this stage of development?

50
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:23,220
 Oh, well, that is a very long story, Piero.

51
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:39,290
 Lead to the same conclusion.

52
00:07:39,490 --> 00:07:41,970
 There is no chance that Captain Piero is still alive.

53
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,970
 There is no logical certainty.

54
00:07:44,410 --> 00:07:46,970
 At the very least, this space landing ship must be found.

55
00:07:47,470 --> 00:07:49,490
 What are your orders, great computer?

56
00:07:49,490 --> 00:07:52,240
 We have other work to do.

57
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:54,430
 Abandon the search for the time being.

58
00:08:01,090 --> 00:08:06,390
 Perhaps you have observed that the annoying clatter of their search vehicles

59
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:08,510
 has not troubled our ears for some time.

60
00:08:10,420 --> 00:08:23,100
 This is his domain, not yours.

61
00:08:24,050 --> 00:08:27,230
 Now, what was that, a Scutasaurus or a Tribectrachus?

62
00:08:27,390 --> 00:08:30,470
 In any case, the poor fellow is well behind his time of throwback.

63
00:08:31,090 --> 00:08:33,230
 Why don't you want to help us?

64
00:08:33,550 --> 00:08:36,270
 You can see for yourself how kind our friends are.

65
00:08:36,490 --> 00:08:39,190
 And I will admit, we do have a special interest in you.

66
00:08:39,330 --> 00:08:40,270
 Naturally, we would.

67
00:08:40,350 --> 00:08:42,590
 After all, you are quite a remarkable young lady.

68
00:08:42,690 --> 00:08:44,950
 looked at from any angle, and you are so gifted.

69
00:08:44,950 --> 00:08:48,000
 We want only to know you better, Psyche.

70
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:51,470
 Say so personally.

71
00:08:51,470 --> 00:08:53,890
 Yes, Psyche, that's right, attractive.

72
00:08:53,890 --> 00:08:56,570
 Soon we'll be the masters of the universe.

73
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:58,680
 You can be queen of the universe.

74
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:00,290
 - You are detestable.

75
00:09:00,290 --> 00:09:01,720
 You're disgusting.

76
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:02,700
 - Be careful, miss.

77
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:04,770
 You should not excite yourself like that.

78
00:09:04,770 --> 00:09:07,270
 You are still in a very delicate state, you know.

79
00:09:07,270 --> 00:09:09,350
 - She's out of her head, such a temper.

80
00:09:09,350 --> 00:09:12,030
 Anyway, now you don't have a great deal of choice.

81
00:09:12,030 --> 00:09:14,380
 You know that, Piero is dead.

82
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:15,820
 - No, that's not true, you're lying.

83
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:17,000
 I know for sure he's alive.

84
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:19,650
 That's very interesting indeed.

85
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:20,290
 Thank you.

86
00:09:20,410 --> 00:09:23,250
 Now we'll send out reconnaissance ships till we find him.

87
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:43,140
 I was telling you, this is where all human life started on this planet.

88
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:45,900
 That's a spaceship.

89
00:09:46,060 --> 00:09:46,910
 How did it get here?

90
00:09:47,010 --> 00:09:47,650
 How long is it?

91
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:49,780
 Yes, it is a spaceship.

92
00:09:50,210 --> 00:09:51,850
 At least it's all that's left of it.

93
00:09:52,250 --> 00:09:52,770
 It's a story.

94
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:56,060
 It all started, I guess, at least five centuries ago.

95
00:09:56,430 --> 00:09:57,680
 A spaceship left Earth.

96
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:00,480
 Aboard were people who were going to settle in new worlds.

97
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,980
 Technology then wasn't what it is today.

98
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:04,620
 Was it pilot error?

99
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,360
 Or an instrument fault?

100
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:09,710
 They were off course, right in the path of an asteroid.

101
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:11,310
 There are so many in this region.

102
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:14,930
 We'll have to change course at once.

103
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:17,360
 All crew, at your stations.

104
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:38,670
 Passengers survived.

105
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,520
 Using what they could find on the craft,

106
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:44,100
 they set about establishing a new life for themselves.

107
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,860
 They had families, and life went on.

108
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:48,620
 You could say they were our ancestors.

109
00:10:49,710 --> 00:10:51,630
 That's where they built their city.

110
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:53,780
 And they were successful,

111
00:10:54,050 --> 00:10:56,450
 despite the harsh climate and the wild creatures.

112
00:10:57,130 --> 00:11:00,750
 About two centuries later, a small spacecraft arrived.

113
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:03,080
 It landed on our big sister planet, Yama.

114
00:11:03,490 --> 00:11:06,540
 There was only one man aboard, a scientist.

115
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:07,980
 He was a bit mad.

116
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:09,820
 At first, everything went well.

117
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,880
 Every so often, he would visit us here.

118
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:16,200
 He even took some of our people to Yama, where life was much easier.

119
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:21,770
 For some reason, he started manufacturing machines.

120
00:11:22,250 --> 00:11:23,730
 Then everything changed for the worse.

121
00:11:24,110 --> 00:11:25,730
 His robots wanted to build a base.

122
00:11:26,230 --> 00:11:27,430
 The people didn't want it.

123
00:11:27,690 --> 00:11:28,460
 It was war.

124
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:38,120
 The humans had to run away and take refuge in the caves,

125
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,660
 and they've been there ever since.

126
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:42,700
 Some became outcasts, bandits, rebels like our parents.

127
00:11:42,880 --> 00:11:46,500
 The jungle reclaimed all in this hostile world with no meaning or purpose.

128
00:11:47,090 --> 00:11:49,510
 And little by little, man sank to the level of beasts.

129
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:53,770
 It is what we are fighting against.

130
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:56,860
 The only island on this planet is their base, their city.

131
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:57,760
 But what a city.

132
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:00,400
 I'll tell you right now, you are going to be impressed.

133
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:08,440
 We'll fire on anything that moves.

134
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:10,000
 You understand?

135
00:12:10,220 --> 00:12:11,340
 Shoot everything.

136
00:12:14,190 --> 00:12:37,470
 Get our mounts back.

137
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,150
 Stop these critters.

138
00:12:43,270 --> 00:12:43,570
 Whoa.

139
00:12:43,710 --> 00:12:45,210
 What is this, a circus or something?

140
00:12:45,250 --> 00:13:50,220
 One good thing out of that.

141
00:13:50,690 --> 00:13:53,190
 Now once and for all, they are convinced that we're dead.

142
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:55,030
 We still have a long way to go.

143
00:13:55,830 --> 00:13:57,470
 If nothing else happens, three days.

144
00:13:58,490 --> 00:14:00,240
 No food and no mounts to ride.

145
00:14:00,530 --> 00:14:02,000
 And our weapons won't function.

146
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:05,450
 And what about me? Forgotten me? As usual.

147
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:06,360
 Metro!

148
00:14:07,630 --> 00:14:09,800
 Metro, good old Metro.

149
00:14:10,010 --> 00:14:12,610
 Thought you were dead while burned, totally destroyed.

150
00:14:13,090 --> 00:14:15,380
 Takes more than a crude ray gun to get your strolly.

151
00:14:15,710 --> 00:14:18,230
 Well, how did you do it? How did you avoid them?

152
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,000
 Oh, it was easy. Nothing brilliant.

153
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:22,400
 I just relaxed and let nature take its course.

154
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:24,410
 The fact is, I didn't have much choice.

155
00:14:25,410 --> 00:14:27,470
 Just as I supposed they walked right past me.

156
00:14:32,730 --> 00:14:33,960
 I was tied down.

157
00:14:34,430 --> 00:14:36,900
 Couldn't have moved if I tried.

158
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:39,390
 To make a short story shorter, here I am,

159
00:14:39,390 --> 00:14:40,900
 but I'm worried about all of you.

160
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,010
 Good for you, Metro.

161
00:14:42,010 --> 00:14:43,840
 You don't know how glad I am to see you.

162
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:47,310
 You do realize that now with me here, you have a weapon.

163
00:14:47,310 --> 00:14:49,860
 You know, it's going to be practically impossible.

164
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:51,160
 No mounts to ride, no food.

165
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:52,170
 It doesn't look good.

166
00:14:52,170 --> 00:14:54,430
 No doubt it has escaped your recollection.

167
00:14:54,430 --> 00:14:58,720
 I can fly.

168
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:06,050
 Yes, my friend, carrying two of us is possible,

169
00:15:06,050 --> 00:15:08,150
 but you could never carry three.

170
00:15:08,150 --> 00:15:09,250
 Both of you go on.

171
00:15:09,250 --> 00:15:11,080
 I can get there alone.

172
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,990
 No, it would be certain death.

173
00:15:12,990 --> 00:15:14,280
 No, out of the question.

174
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:16,890
 We started out together, and we're going on together.

175
00:15:23,140 --> 00:15:28,060
 Stop here. We'll wait here till nightfall. It'll be less dangerous.

176
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:35,010
 Wing, wing, wing, wing. Wake up, my children. Time to get up.

177
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:45,150
 Tell me, is it much farther?

178
00:15:45,630 --> 00:15:47,660
 Tomorrow night, with luck, we might be there.

179
00:15:47,930 --> 00:15:49,590
 If we can hold out till then.

180
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:52,220
 But there's a new danger with every step.

181
00:15:52,510 --> 00:15:58,510
 Around their city, ferocious beasts roam wild, and there are armed groups, bandits who live on plunder and pillage.

182
00:15:58,790 --> 00:16:00,350
 And the government doesn't do anything?

183
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:02,480
 They cast a blind eye.

184
00:16:03,230 --> 00:16:07,310
 Barbarism, they don't care. All that matters to them is their base, the Astroport.

185
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:09,650
 Aside from that, the occasional police patrol.

186
00:16:10,150 --> 00:16:11,830
 Just to show that they're in control.

187
00:16:20,530 --> 00:16:27,090
 Still more of them!

188
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:48,130
 The sky's cleared, the attacker's captured, that's good work.

189
00:16:48,610 --> 00:16:49,220
 Do you agree?

190
00:16:49,430 --> 00:16:51,740
 I call that coming to help fellow human.

191
00:16:53,230 --> 00:16:57,870
 Rich here, why don't you give us a nice little gift to show how grateful.

192
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:05,250
 Little gold, nice little ray gunner, if you don't mind.

193
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:22,140
 No, not much value here.

194
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,320
 I don't suppose you've got anything better to give us.

195
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:26,940
 No, one look at you and me, I can see you don't.

196
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:30,540
 But you yourselves, maybe you're valuable to somebody.

197
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:32,920
 Why would you be risking your necks here?

198
00:17:47,670 --> 00:17:48,490
 Take a rest now.

199
00:17:48,590 --> 00:17:50,530
 I wouldn't want to damage the merchandise.

200
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:52,170
 You're valuable to someone.

201
00:17:57,030 --> 00:17:58,140
 Oh, funny bits.

202
00:17:59,550 --> 00:18:02,550
 These guys are the fastest shots in the Western galaxy.

203
00:18:02,670 --> 00:18:06,580
 I wouldn't tempt...

204
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:09,070
 Hungry! Look at them!

205
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:13,210
 Still don't want to tell me what you're doing here.

206
00:18:13,430 --> 00:18:13,670
 Hmm?

207
00:18:13,890 --> 00:18:15,230
 Or who you all are.

208
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,700
 Say why you were walking in this area.

209
00:18:17,890 --> 00:18:20,130
 Don't worry. We'll find out.

210
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:23,570
 Our leader knows lots of ways to make people talk.

211
00:18:23,860 --> 00:18:27,510
 But I'll be a monkey's uncle if you aren't very valuable to someone someplace.

212
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:29,810
 And that kid's toy, too.

213
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:36,090
 One thing's for sure, this little beauty right here.

214
00:18:36,430 --> 00:18:38,470
 She's going to be very interesting to our leader.

215
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:42,370
 Cool it, you don't want me to get angry, kid.

216
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,910
 What's the matter? Can't you tell when it's a joke?

217
00:18:45,050 --> 00:18:46,610
 How can we have a conversation?

218
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:49,040
 You won't say anything, and it's not my fault.

219
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:52,520
 You understand you realize the favor that we did you.

220
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:55,330
 It isn't easy to get rid of those flying things.

221
00:18:55,390 --> 00:18:56,290
 You saw what they're like.

222
00:18:57,610 --> 00:18:59,330
 I'll tell you it's an interesting story.

223
00:18:59,330 --> 00:19:02,360
 We learned that little trick from the castle guys.

224
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:05,170
 That's how they used to grab people on the ground.

225
00:19:05,570 --> 00:19:08,670
 Our leaders learned all that kind of goodies from those castle guys.

226
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:12,020
 Tell me, your leader, who is he?

227
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:13,390
 Ah, that's a question.

228
00:19:13,730 --> 00:19:14,730
 Now it's my turn.

229
00:19:14,830 --> 00:19:16,050
 That's going to be a mystery.

230
00:19:16,310 --> 00:19:18,430
 If he wants you to know, he'll tell you.

231
00:19:18,650 --> 00:19:20,330
 Now that you've had a rest, let's get going.

232
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:34,310
 Quandary, my friend.

233
00:19:34,510 --> 00:19:39,170
 Not sure whether I should slice them like cold ham or quietly boil away here.

234
00:19:39,230 --> 00:19:40,050
 It's difficult to tell.

235
00:19:40,630 --> 00:19:41,280
 No, Metro.

236
00:19:41,420 --> 00:19:42,860
 Basically, they're good guys.

237
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,140
 Right now, we're not in danger.

238
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,010
 Anyway, we mustn't hurt them.

239
00:19:47,110 --> 00:19:47,570
 They're human.

240
00:19:48,140 --> 00:19:48,440
 Oh?

241
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:55,780
 Occasionally, your logic escapes me completely. Oh, well.

242
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:15,220
 It's the capital. Dream city.

243
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:17,570
 First, we have to take a little detour.

244
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:21,620
 The plane's much too dangerous for hard-working, honest folks like us.

245
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:41,120
 Nice pets, wouldn't they?

246
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:44,950
 Nice in here, right? We'd all like to stay here a long time.

247
00:20:45,150 --> 00:20:46,850
 All right, go ahead and untie their hands.

248
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:49,130
 They want to stay with us. They won't go.

249
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:59,930
 Gotta get used to them, though. All right, let's go.

250
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:24,880
 You brought us this leader.

251
00:21:25,650 --> 00:21:29,510
 Hero, that's him, the man we're looking for. Murdoch.

252
00:21:29,510 --> 00:21:36,600
 Be well, we'll take good care of you, but I expect you to play fair with us.

253
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:40,760
 We want to know who you are and who's willing to pay the highest price for you.

254
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:44,350
 The ones at the Astropark, Yama Castle, let's go, I want to know, and now.

255
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:48,720
 It's you I came here to see. They only came along to show me the way, they were only guides.

256
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:51,680
 All this way, just to see me? That's what I call a great honor.

257
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:53,620
 Now suppose you tell me why you came.

258
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:55,550
 You have to take me to Yama.

259
00:21:56,860 --> 00:22:01,200
 To Yama, that's all you want? How do you think I could get you there, huh?

260
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:05,290
 Aboard your spacecraft, you're the only one on this whole planet who can.

261
00:22:05,610 --> 00:22:07,600
 You're well informed, I see, all right.

262
00:22:07,780 --> 00:22:08,720
 Let's say you're right.

263
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:10,140
 Why should I take you there?

264
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:11,260
 Can you pay me for it?

265
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:11,840
 No, nothing.

266
00:22:12,340 --> 00:22:15,020
 Well, here everything's paid for and everything has its price.

267
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:17,340
 Your life, my life, theirs.

268
00:22:17,700 --> 00:22:20,520
 And even this thing here, I don't know what you call it,

269
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:22,380
 but it reminds me of some bad memories.

270
00:22:22,860 --> 00:22:25,130
 I'm from the Omega Intergalactic Police,

271
00:22:25,230 --> 00:22:26,770
 and we're fighting your oppressors.

272
00:22:27,540 --> 00:22:29,210
 Ah, the valiant fighter.

273
00:22:29,210 --> 00:22:29,990
 Here he is.

274
00:22:30,090 --> 00:22:32,070
 The face of the planet is going to change.

275
00:22:32,210 --> 00:22:32,990
 Look around you.

276
00:22:33,670 --> 00:22:34,690
 Look around you.

277
00:22:35,580 --> 00:22:38,440
 We are the mountain people, Murdoch.

278
00:22:38,730 --> 00:22:39,830
 What he says is true.

279
00:22:39,970 --> 00:22:42,610
 We found him when his spacecraft crashed in our region.

280
00:22:42,910 --> 00:22:45,050
 We brought him back to health and guided him here.

281
00:22:45,190 --> 00:22:45,950
 You must help him.

282
00:22:46,230 --> 00:22:48,630
 Ah, more noble words, you mountain people.

283
00:22:48,730 --> 00:22:49,750
 You're all idealists.

284
00:22:49,830 --> 00:22:50,770
 I honor you for that.

285
00:22:50,870 --> 00:22:51,650
 I wish you well.

286
00:22:51,710 --> 00:22:52,870
 I've proved that many times.

287
00:22:53,050 --> 00:22:54,490
 But your struggle is not mine.

288
00:22:54,590 --> 00:22:56,250
 This world isn't going to change overnight.

289
00:22:56,550 --> 00:22:58,290
 What do you want me to do with our hero?

290
00:22:58,290 --> 00:23:00,270
 I'll sell him to Yama if they're interested

291
00:23:00,270 --> 00:23:02,670
 and if they agree to pay me enough for him.

292
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:06,090
 I thought you were a leader.

293
00:23:06,190 --> 00:23:07,050
 You're only a slave.

294
00:23:07,250 --> 00:23:09,930
 and you will never rise to anything higher, Murdoch.

295
00:23:11,540 --> 00:23:15,780
 Never talk to me like that again, kid.

296
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:18,560
 Guys like you, I've crushed with my bare hands for less.

297
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:20,680
 Here, look. See that?

298
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:23,130
 Do they look like the scars of a slave?

299
00:23:23,750 --> 00:23:30,910
 Do they? Get them out of here.

300
00:23:57,050 --> 00:24:05,990
 Understand how important it is, all that's happening here?

301
00:24:06,220 --> 00:24:09,880
 If we let them win, there won't be place for man anywhere in the universe.

302
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:11,930
 There won't be any hope.

303
00:24:12,170 --> 00:24:13,270
 Doesn't that matter to you?

304
00:24:13,270 --> 00:24:15,200
 A man worthy of a name,

305
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:18,210
 can he remain indifferent when humanity itself is at stake?

306
00:24:18,830 --> 00:24:20,670
 Our Confederation is fighting against them.

307
00:24:20,780 --> 00:24:23,460
 If we win, your world can once again be civilized.

308
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:24,760
 Take your place beside us.

309
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:27,040
 You will once again join your fellow human.

310
00:24:27,560 --> 00:24:28,430
 Do you believe it?

311
00:24:28,880 --> 00:24:30,350
 Is that true what he said, Chief?

312
00:24:30,710 --> 00:24:34,350
 The Confederation of Omega, does it really exist?

313
00:24:35,700 --> 00:24:37,950
 You know something, kid, I like you.

314
00:24:38,220 --> 00:24:39,630
 Because you've got guts.

315
00:24:39,850 --> 00:24:42,750
 And if you want to know, we don't like those castle guys much.

316
00:24:42,890 --> 00:24:44,590
 In fact, we hate what they do to us.

317
00:24:44,800 --> 00:24:45,850
 That's two reasons.

318
00:24:46,300 --> 00:24:50,190
 Strange as me seem to you, you've given me no choice but to help you.

319
00:24:50,590 --> 00:24:57,190
 I shall never understand them.

320
00:25:00,860 --> 00:25:05,750
 wondering this ship used to belong to them we borrowed it a while back they

321
00:25:05,750 --> 00:25:16,770
 won't pay any attention to us the truth is we've fiddled a bit and this is what

322
00:25:16,770 --> 00:25:39,290
 you call your spaceship patience captain you watch and you'll see

